window.__CAPM_DATA=(window.__CAPM_DATA||"")+"\\\"/><\\/div>\",\"stemText\":\"Match the statements concerning the tasks of a hybrid project with their right classification:\",\"choices\":[],\"key\":[],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sBZ-1\\\">Correct <span><\\/span>Answer:<\\/p><div class=\\\"class_s76-0\\\"><img alt=\\\"Source figure\\\" loading=\\\"lazy\\\" src=\\\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\\\"/><\\/div><ol class=\\\"class_s7K-1\\\"><li><p>Task A is not yet complete: Data. Work performance data is the raw measurements and observations made during project execution (PMI - Process groups guide, page 23). <\\/p><\\/li><\\/ol><ol class=\\\"class_s7K-1\\\" start=\\\"2\\\"><li><p>Task B is not accepted because of a security issue: Information. When data is analyzed, it becomes information. <\\/p><\\/li><\\/ol><ol class=\\\"class_s7K-1\\\" start=\\\"3\\\"><li><p>Task C had a huge impact on the burndown chart: Report. Examining the whole picture in a burndown chart is a form of reporting. <\\/p><\\/li><\\/ol><ol class=\\\"class_s7K-1\\\" start=\\\"4\\\"><li><p>Task D is added to the product backlog based on customer feedback: Practice. The activity of creating, refining, estimating, and prioritizing product backlog items is one of the agile practices. <\\/p><\\/li><\\/ol>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer: Task A is not yet complete: Data. Work performance data is the raw measurements and observations made during project execution (PMI - Process groups guide, page 23). Task B is not accepted because of a security issue: Information. When data is analyzed, it becomes information. Task C had a huge impact on the burndown chart: Report. Examining the whole picture in a burndown chart is a form of reporting. Task D is added to the product backlog based on customer feedback: Practice. The activity of creating, refining, estimating, and prioritizing product backlog items is one of the agile practices.\",\"type\":\"mapping\",\"special\":{\"type\":\"mapping\",\"targets\":[[\"A\",\"A. Task A is not yet complete\"],[\"B\",\"B. Task B is not accepted because of a security issue\"],[\"C\",\"C. Task C had a huge impact on the burndown chart\"],[\"D\",\"D. Task D is added to the product backlog based on customer feedback\"]],\"options\":[[\"report\",\"Report\"],[\"data\",\"Data\"],[\"practice\",\"Practice\"],[\"information\",\"Information\"]],\"correct\":{\"A\":\"data\",\"B\":\"information\",\"C\":\"report\",\"D\":\"practice\"}},\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":86,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">During a sprint planning, a team member mentioned that some events were missing. What should the project manager add? (Select three)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"During a sprint planning, a team member mentioned that some events were missing. What should the project manager add? (Select three)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Daily scrum<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Daily scrum\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Increments<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Increments\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Retrospectives<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Retrospectives\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Sprint review<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Sprint review\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>Product backlo<span><\\/span>g<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. Product backlo g\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"C\",\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A, C, D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The Daily Scrum is a brief, time-boxed meeting held each day during a sprint, typically lasting 15 minutes. Its purpose is to provide a regular opportunity for the Scrum team to synchronize their work, discuss progress, and plan the day’s activities. A retrospective is a recurring workshop where participants reflect on their work and outcomes to enhance both the process and the product. It serves as a structured opportunity for team members to evaluate what went well, identify areas for improvement, and apply lessons learned to future sprints. A Sprint Review, or Iteration Review, is conducted at the conclusion of each iteration to showcase and evaluate the work completed. This meeting provides an opportunity to demonstrate the results achieved during the iteration and gather feedback from stakeholders.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A, C, D The Daily Scrum is a brief, time-boxed meeting held each day during a sprint, typically lasting 15 minutes. Its purpose is to provide a regular opportunity for the Scrum team to synchronize their work, discuss progress, and plan the day’s activities. A retrospective is a recurring workshop where participants reflect on their work and outcomes to enhance both the process and the product. It serves as a structured opportunity for team members to evaluate what went well, identify areas for improvement, and apply lessons learned to future sprints. A Sprint Review, or Iteration Review, is conducted at the conclusion of each iteration to showcase and evaluate the work completed. This meeting provides an opportunity to demonstrate the results achieved during the iteration and gather feedback from stakeholders.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":3},{\"n\":87,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager is managing a project using a hybrid approach. After one week of the first iteration, the customer informed the project manager that they were dissatisfied with the deliverables. What should the project manager do next?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is managing a project using a hybrid approach. After one week of the first iteration, the customer informed the project manager that they were dissatisfied with the deliverables. What should the project manager do next?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Ask the customer to submit a change request so that their dissatisfaction can be addressed<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Ask the customer to submit a change request so that their dissatisfaction can be addressed\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Use soft skills to convince the customer that the deliverables conform to project specifications<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Use soft skills to convince the customer that the deliverables conform to project specifications\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Investigate the cause of dissatisfaction and verify the deliverables<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Investigate the cause of dissatisfaction and verify the deliverables\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Implement adjustments and improvements in the next iteration<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Implement adjustments and improvements in the next iteration\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The first thing the project manager should do is listen to the customer, take note of the reasons behind their dissatisfaction, and verify the deliverables. Once this is done, the project manager will be equipped with all of the needed information to make the best decision. If they realize that it’s just a misunderstanding or the customer is missing some details regarding the project deliverables, then they can simply use their soft skills to explain and convince them that the deliverables are good. However, if the deliverables do not meet specifications or require improvement, then they should plan to implement changes in the upcoming iterations according to the priorities set by the customer. Since the project is hybrid, the project manager may also need to ask the customer to submit a change request if out-of-scope work is requested.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The first thing the project manager should do is listen to the customer, take note of the reasons behind their dissatisfaction, and verify the deliverables. Once this is done, the project manager will be equipped with all of the needed information to make the best decision. If they realize that it’s just a misunderstanding or the customer is missing some details regarding the project deliverables, then they can simply use their soft skills to explain and convince them that the deliverables are good. However, if the deliverables do not meet specifications or require improvement, then they should plan to implement changes in the upcoming iterations according to the priorities set by the customer. Since the project is hybrid, the project manager may also need to ask the customer to submit a change request if out-of-scope work is requested.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":88,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2A3-0\\\">To take into consideration the Triple Bottom Line, the project manager invites the sponsor to attend a meeting to define the scope of a new project. What are the three elements of the Triple Bottom Line?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"To take into consideration the Triple Bottom Line, the project manager invites the sponsor to attend a meeting to define the scope of a new project. What are the three elements of the Triple Bottom Line?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1BZ-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>Performance, planet, profit<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Performance, planet, profit\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Plan, people, profit<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Plan, people, profit\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Profit, people, planet<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Profit, people, planet\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Profit, people, performance<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Profit, people, performance\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2A1-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s4JX\\\">The Triple Bottom Line (TBL) is a sustainability framework for evaluating a company's bottom line from the perspectives of profit, people, and the planet (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 252). This concept implies that companies should commit to measuring their social and environmental impact, in addition to their financial performance, rather than solely focusing on generating profit.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The Triple Bottom Line (TBL) is a sustainability framework for evaluating a company's bottom line from the perspectives of profit, people, and the planet (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 252). This concept implies that companies should commit to measuring their social and environmental impact, in addition to their financial performance, rather than solely focusing on generating profit.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":89,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">A project manager is in charge of the creation of an online catalog of the company’s products. A particular team member is managing documentation. Even though this member is doing a great job, their work pace is way slower than expected, which can cause the whole project to miss its deadline. What should the project manager do first in this situation? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is in charge of the creation of an online catalog of the company’s products. A particular team member is managing documentation. Even though this member is doing a great job, their work pace is way slower than expected, which can cause the whole project to miss its deadline. What should the project manager do first in this situation?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1BZ-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>Delegate some of the concerned team member’s tasks to other writers<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Delegate some of the concerned team member’s tasks to other writers\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Remove the concerned team member from the project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Remove the concerned team member from the project\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Find out the cause of the team member’s slow work pace<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Find out the cause of the team member’s slow work pace\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Give the concerned team member other non-critical tasks<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Give the concerned team member other non-critical tasks\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\"><span>Correct Answer = C<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\" id=\\\"page_177\\\">Before taking any corrective measures, the project manager should determine the underlying cause of the problem. If it turns out that the concerned team member is overallocated. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> It might be better to assign some of the team member’s work to other writers. However, the concerned team member is doing a great job, regardless of their slow work pace. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Removing the team member from the project can have a negative impact on the quality of the deliverables. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Assigning the team member to non-critical tasks can have a bad impact on their motivation, plus it does not resolve the main problem, i.e. their slow work pace. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Before taking any corrective measures, the project manager should determine the underlying cause of the problem. If it turns out that the concerned team member is overallocated. Option A: It might be better to assign some of the team member’s work to other writers. However, the concerned team member is doing a great job, regardless of their slow work pace. Option B: Removing the team member from the project can have a negative impact on the quality of the deliverables. Option D: Assigning the team member to non-critical tasks can have a bad impact on their motivation, plus it does not resolve the main problem, i.e. their slow work pace.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":90,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager has completed the first phase of a project. What should the project manager do next?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager has completed the first phase of a project. What should the project manager do next?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Arrange a phase review with the customer<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Arrange a phase review with the customer\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Close the project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Close the project\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Approve the first phase<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Approve the first phase\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Start the second phase<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Start the second phase\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Phase reviews, aka phase gates, phase exits, phase entrances, and stage gates, is a formal review of the project to evaluate its status. The results are documented and presented to the concerned stakeholders or the sponsor in order to get their approval to proceed to the next phase in the project lifecycle (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 244).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Phase reviews, aka phase gates, phase exits, phase entrances, and stage gates, is a formal review of the project to evaluate its status. The results are documented and presented to the concerned stakeholders or the sponsor in order to get their approval to proceed to the next phase in the project lifecycle (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 244).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":91,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager is leading a project using an iterative development approach. During which meeting is a potentially shippable product increment presented to the concerned stakeholders?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is leading a project using an iterative development approach. During which meeting is a potentially shippable product increment presented to the concerned stakeholders?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Iteration kickoff meeting<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Iteration kickoff meeting\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Iteration planning meeting<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Iteration planning meeting\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Iteration review meeting<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Iteration review meeting\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Iteration retrospective meetin<span><\\/span>g<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Iteration retrospective meetin g\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The project team is expected to deliver shippable product features by the end of each iteration. During the Iteration Review meeting, the project team demonstrates their work to the product owner and concerned stakeholders, in order to get feedback and approval (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 179).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The project team is expected to deliver shippable product features by the end of each iteration. During the Iteration Review meeting, the project team demonstrates their work to the product owner and concerned stakeholders, in order to get feedback and approval (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 179).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":92,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Which practices are essential for effective business stewardship? (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which practices are essential for effective business stewardship? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Staffing more business analysts<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Staffing more business analysts\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Promote business analysis effectiveness<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Promote business analysis effectiveness\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>Implementing a project management office (PMO)<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Implementing a project management office (PMO)\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>Enhance business analysis capability<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Enhance business analysis capability\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Maintaining the status quo in business processes<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Maintaining the status quo in business processes\"}],\"key\":[\"B\",\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = B &amp; D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Promoting business analysis effectiveness involves fostering a mindset of continuous improvement and growth. This mindset encourages business analysts to identify opportunities to adapt processes and tools, aiming to deliver maximum value based on organizational needs. Enhancing business analysis capability through the language, practices, and tools of business analysis within the organization, making them more familiar and effective (Business Analysis for Practitioners, page 93).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Hiring more business analysts without having a goal to improve business processes will not make business stewardship more effective.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Implementing a PMO could contribute to the effectiveness of business stewardship, however the PMO is not an essential practice. Not all organizations have the business need or the adequate size to set up a PMO.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option E:<\\/span> Maintaining the status quo in business processes contradicts the idea of stewardship, which involves ensuring that business analysis practices evolve and improve over time. Maintaining the status quo does not align with the goal of enhancing effectiveness or capability.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B & D Promoting business analysis effectiveness involves fostering a mindset of continuous improvement and growth. This mindset encourages business analysts to identify opportunities to adapt processes and tools, aiming to deliver maximum value based on organizational needs. Enhancing business analysis capability through the language, practices, and tools of business analysis within the organization, making them more familiar and effective (Business Analysis for Practitioners, page 93). Option A: Hiring more business analysts without having a goal to improve business processes will not make business stewardship more effective. Option C: Implementing a PMO could contribute to the effectiveness of business stewardship, however the PMO is not an essential practice. Not all organizations have the business need or the adequate size to set up a PMO. Option E: Maintaining the status quo in business processes contradicts the idea of stewardship, which involves ensuring that business analysis practices evolve and improve over time. Maintaining the status quo does not align with the goal of enhancing effectiveness or capability.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":93,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">A subcontractor is engaged to install the electrical wiring of a construction project. A stakeholder requests a modification in the project's scope, which will result in a change in the subcontractor’s workload. Which of the following documents will address how the change in the subcontractor's workload will be handled? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A subcontractor is engaged to install the electrical wiring of a construction project. A stakeholder requests a modification in the project's scope, which will result in a change in the subcontractor’s workload. Which of the following documents will address how the change in the subcontractor's workload will be handled?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1BZ-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>The change control system<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The change control system\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The procurement management plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The procurement management plan\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The contract<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The contract\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The scope<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The scope\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\"><span>Correct Answer = C<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\" id=\\\"page_178\\\">The contract comprises all of the other mentioned documents. Any changes to any of the predetermined contract terms between the subcontractor and the project manager, including the defined scope of work, should be addressed in the contract. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The change control system doesn’t also define the relationship between the vendor and the project. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The procurement management plan is used to define the process of what, when, and how to acquire material or services from third parties. Yet, it doesn’t define the contractual engagement with each of them. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The scope only reflects the change in the workload but it does not address how this change will impact other aspects (Fee increase, change of completion date, etc.). <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C The contract comprises all of the other mentioned documents. Any changes to any of the predetermined contract terms between the subcontractor and the project manager, including the defined scope of work, should be addressed in the contract. Option A: The change control system doesn’t also define the relationship between the vendor and the project. Option B: The procurement management plan is used to define the process of what, when, and how to acquire material or services from third parties. Yet, it doesn’t define the contractual engagement with each of them. Option D: The scope only reflects the change in the workload but it does not address how this change will impact other aspects (Fee increase, change of completion date, etc.).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":94,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">During a sprint review meeting, a team member demonstrated a new feature and pointed out that it took longer than expected due to missing technical documentation. Then, they asked a senior team member how they could avoid this in the future. What should the meeting facilitator do?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"During a sprint review meeting, a team member demonstrated a new feature and pointed out that it took longer than expected due to missing technical documentation. Then, they asked a senior team member how they could avoid this in the future. What should the meeting facilitator do?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Let the discussion flow naturally since it’s important and only intervene if the side discussion continues for too long<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Let the discussion flow naturally since it’s important and only intervene if the side discussion continues for too long\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Ask the team member to reflect on how to make such improvements at another meeting<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Ask the team member to reflect on how to make such improvements at another meeting\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Interrupt the team member because the product owner is not supposed to know that documentation is missing<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Interrupt the team member because the product owner is not supposed to know that documentation is missing\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Let the discussion continue and then ask the product owner to give feedback on potential improvements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Let the discussion continue and then ask the product owner to give feedback on potential improvements\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The retrospective meeting is the right meeting to reflect on what happened during the sprint and how to improve the implemented processes. Therefore, rather than discussing how to improve future work efficiency, the meeting facilitator should steer back the discussion to only focus on the demonstrated feature and get the product owner’s feedback on what has been produced. This being said, if the documentation needs improvement, team members should create a technical task for it and demonstrate its importance to the product owner during Sprint Planning.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The retrospective meeting is the right meeting to reflect on what happened during the sprint and how to improve the implemented processes. Therefore, rather than discussing how to improve future work efficiency, the meeting facilitator should steer back the discussion to only focus on the demonstrated feature and get the product owner’s feedback on what has been produced. This being said, if the documentation needs improvement, team members should create a technical task for it and demonstrate its importance to the product owner during Sprint Planning.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":95,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Which of the following may lead to changes in the product scope?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following may lead to changes in the product scope?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Approval of the business case<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Approval of the business case\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Changes in the scope management plan<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Changes in the scope management plan\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>Completion of the project charter<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Completion of the project charter\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>Evolving business needs, risks, or constraints<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Evolving business needs, risks, or constraints\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9D-0\\\">Once the business case is approved, the chosen solution approach sets the initial product scope. At this stage, the product scope is defined broadly by the capabilities and features linked to the selected option. As the product team conducts further analysis, the product scope is continuously refined. During the initiative, the product scope may be adjusted to accommodate evolving business needs, emerging risks, or constraints related to budget or schedule. (PMI guide to business analysis, page 103)<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Once the business case is approved, the chosen solution approach sets the initial product scope. At this stage, the product scope is defined broadly by the capabilities and features linked to the selected option. As the product team conducts further analysis, the product scope is continuously refined. During the initiative, the product scope may be adjusted to accommodate evolving business needs, emerging risks, or constraints related to budget or schedule. (PMI guide to business analysis, page 103)\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":96,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A team has 100 story points in the product backlog and a velocity of 30 points per iteration. Taking into consideration that the iteration is two weeks long, how many weeks does the team need to complete the backlog?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A team has 100 story points in the product backlog and a velocity of 30 points per iteration. Taking into consideration that the iteration is two weeks long, how many weeks does the team need to complete the backlog?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>4 weeks<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. 4 weeks\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>6 week<span><\\/span>s<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. 6 week s\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>8 weeks<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. 8 weeks\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>10 weeks<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. 10 weeks\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">It will take the project team 3.3 iterations to complete the backlog work items:<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">(100 story points / 30 story points = 3.3 iterations)<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">It would take 4 iterations to complete the work because the timebox of the iteration shouldn’t be changed. Since the question is how many weeks are needed to complete work, then 8 weeks is the right answer.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C It will take the project team 3.3 iterations to complete the backlog work items: (100 story points / 30 story points = 3.3 iterations) It would take 4 iterations to complete the work because the timebox of the iteration shouldn’t be changed. Since the question is how many weeks are needed to complete work, then 8 weeks is the right answer.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":97,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">The Earned Value (EV) is less than the Planned Value (PV). What does this mean?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"The Earned Value (EV) is less than the Planned Value (PV). What does this mean?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The cost variance is positive, the project is under budget<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The cost variance is positive, the project is under budget\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The cost variance is negative, the project is over budget<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The cost variance is negative, the project is over budget\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The schedule variance is positive, the project is ahead of schedule<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The schedule variance is positive, the project is ahead of schedule\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The schedule variance is negative, the project is behind schedule<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The schedule variance is negative, the project is behind schedule\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Schedule Variance (SV) is a measure of schedule performance. It’s calculated through the difference between the Earned Value and Planned Value (SV = EV - PV). When the SV is negative, it indicates that the project is behind what was initially planned. When the SV is positive, it indicates that the project is ahead of what was originally planned.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Schedule Variance (SV) is a measure of schedule performance. It’s calculated through the difference between the Earned Value and Planned Value (SV = EV - PV). When the SV is negative, it indicates that the project is behind what was initially planned. When the SV is positive, it indicates that the project is ahead of what was originally planned.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":98,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">What can a project manager use Source Selection criteria for? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What can a project manager use Source Selection criteria for?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3C-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project performance assessment <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Project performance assessment\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Quality compliance inspection <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Quality compliance inspection\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Sellers assessment <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Sellers assessment\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Potential projects evaluation <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Potential projects evaluation\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\" id=\\\"page_179\\\"><span>Correct Answer = C<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\">Source Selection Criteria is a valuable tool for choosing a qualified seller from a short list of potential candidates. This method can help the buyer ensure that the selected seller will offer the best quality for the products or services required. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Source Selection Criteria is a valuable tool for choosing a qualified seller from a short list of potential candidates. This method can help the buyer ensure that the selected seller will offer the best quality for the products or services required.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":99,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">A project manager is leading a 3-year project that involves upgrading and improving an electric engine for industrial use. Since the majority of the project activities are hazardous, the project team will receive extensive safety training. The training will ensure the safety of workers and prevent delays caused by unsatisfactory work. The cost of the conducted safety training falls under: <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is leading a 3-year project that involves upgrading and improving an electric engine for industrial use. Since the majority of the project activities are hazardous, the project team will receive extensive safety training. The training will ensure the safety of workers and prevent delays caused by unsatisfactory work. The cost of the conducted safety training falls under:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1BZ-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>Cost of regulations<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Cost of regulations\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Cost of Quality<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Cost of Quality\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Cost of conformance<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Cost of conformance\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Cost of nonconformance<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Cost of nonconformance\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2A1-0\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A3-0\\\">Training costs fall under the cost of conformance to quality.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A5-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The described scenario does not mention that the training was conducted to comply with certain regulations.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A5-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The cost of quality is too generic as an answer since it comprises both the Cost of Conformance and the Cost of non-conformance.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A5-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The cost of nonconformance involves the cost of internal and external failure costs, which is not the case here.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Training costs fall under the cost of conformance to quality. Option A: The described scenario does not mention that the training was conducted to comply with certain regulations. Option B: The cost of quality is too generic as an answer since it comprises both the Cost of Conformance and the Cost of non-conformance. Option D: The cost of nonconformance involves the cost of internal and external failure costs, which is not the case here.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":100,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager is in charge of a project for creating a next-generation vehicle. Before the assembly of the vehicle can be performed, the wheels have to be designed and built. Which type of dependency does this situation depict?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is in charge of a project for creating a next-generation vehicle. Before the assembly of the vehicle can be performed, the wheels have to be designed and built. Which type of dependency does this situation depict?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>External<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. External\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Discretionary<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Discretionary\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Soft Logic<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Soft Logic\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Mandatory<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Mandatory\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A mandatory dependency is also called a hard dependency or hard logic. For example, consider 2 activities A and B, if B has a mandatory dependency on A, it means action on B cannot be performed until action on A has been completed.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> External dependencies involve a relationship between project activities and non-project activities (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 60).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> A discretionary or soft logic dependency, on the other hand, is an optional or preferred dependency.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D A mandatory dependency is also called a hard dependency or hard logic. For example, consider 2 activities A and B, if B has a mandatory dependency on A, it means action on B cannot be performed until action on A has been completed. Option A: External dependencies involve a relationship between project activities and non-project activities (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 60). Option B: A discretionary or soft logic dependency, on the other hand, is an optional or preferred dependency.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":101,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">During a meeting with stakeholders, the project manager is asked about the amount of work completed by the agile team during the last sprint. What information should the project manager share with stakeholders?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"During a meeting with stakeholders, the project manager is asked about the amount of work completed by the agile team during the last sprint. What information should the project manager share with stakeholders?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The sprint velocity<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The sprint velocity\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The sprint backlog items<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The sprint backlog items\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The average velocit<span><\\/span>y<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The average velocit y\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The forecasting velocity<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The forecasting velocity\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Velocity is the sum of the story point sizes for the features actually completed in this iteration. Velocity allows the team to plan its next capacity more accurately by looking at its historical performance (Agile practice guide, page 64).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The sprint backlog is a list of product backlog items pulled into a sprint, which may not be completed by the end of the sprint.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Average velocity represents the average velocity of all the previous sprints.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The forecasting velocity is used when the team is new to the Agile approach and has no historical data.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Velocity is the sum of the story point sizes for the features actually completed in this iteration. Velocity allows the team to plan its next capacity more accurately by looking at its historical performance (Agile practice guide, page 64). Option A: The sprint backlog is a list of product backlog items pulled into a sprint, which may not be completed by the end of the sprint. Option C: Average velocity represents the average velocity of all the previous sprints. Option D: The forecasting velocity is used when the team is new to the Agile approach and has no historical data.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":102,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">During a retrospective meeting, two team members disagree about their involvement in a recent work incident, accusing each other of dodging responsibility. To avoid such an issue in the future, the project manager decides to create a RACI matrix. RACI is an acronym for:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"During a retrospective meeting, two team members disagree about their involvement in a recent work incident, accusing each other of dodging responsibility. To avoid such an issue in the future, the project manager decides to create a RACI matrix. RACI is an acronym for:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Responsible, Accountable, Confirm, Inform<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Responsible, Accountable, Confirm, Inform\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Recommended, Accountable, Consulted, Inform<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Recommended, Accountable, Consulted, Inform\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Responsible, Accountant, Consulted, Inform<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Responsible, Accountant, Consulted, Inform\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Responsible, Accountable, Consulted, Inform<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Responsible, Accountable, Consulted, Inform\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">RACI stands for Responsible, Accountable, Consulted, Inform. The RACI chart or matrix is an example of the Responsibility Assignment Matrix (RAM), which shows the relationship between <span><\\/span>activities and team members as it defines team members’ roles and responsibilities. It’s an efficient tool to make sure everyone is on the same page and understands what they are supposed to do.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D RACI stands for Responsible, Accountable, Consulted, Inform. The RACI chart or matrix is an example of the Responsibility Assignment Matrix (RAM), which shows the relationship between activities and team members as it defines team members’ roles and responsibilities. It’s an efficient tool to make sure everyone is on the same page and understands what they are supposed to do.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":103,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">Establishing a change control system is crucial for a project’s success. The coordination of all changes across the whole project is part of change control. When should integrated change control be performed? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Establishing a change control system is crucial for a project’s success. The coordination of all changes across the whole project is part of change control. When should integrated change control be performed?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1BZ-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>Throughout the whole project<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Throughout the whole project\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>During the project execution phase<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. During the project execution phase\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>During the planning phase<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. During the planning phase\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>During the monitoring and controlling phase<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. During the monitoring and controlling phase\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2A1-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A3-0\\\">Integrated change control should be performed throughout the whole project, from start to finish. Integrated change control is the process of reviewing all change requests, approving or rejecting changes, and managing implemented changes. Therefore, it should not be limited to a specific process group or project phase.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Integrated change control should be performed throughout the whole project, from start to finish. Integrated change control is the process of reviewing all change requests, approving or rejecting changes, and managing implemented changes. Therefore, it should not be limited to a specific process group or project phase.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":104,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">An organization puts too much emphasis on continuous improvement. In which of the following meetings can the organization teams discuss why things went wrong and what could be improved? (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"An organization puts too much emphasis on continuous improvement. In which of the following meetings can the organization teams discuss why things went wrong and what could be improved? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Retrospective meeting<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Retrospective meeting\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Lessons learned meeting<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Lessons learned meeting\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Status meeting<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Status meeting\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Review meeting<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Review meeting\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A &amp; B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Lessons learned are known as retrospectives (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 71). This meeting is used to check what went wrong and what could be improved.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> A status meeting is held to review the actual status as well as risks. Status meetings could be eventually followed by preventive or corrective actions, change requests, or lessons learned meetings.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> A review meeting is held to check or demonstrate deliverables.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A & B Lessons learned are known as retrospectives (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 71). This meeting is used to check what went wrong and what could be improved. Option C: A status meeting is held to review the actual status as well as risks. Status meetings could be eventually followed by preventive or corrective actions, change requests, or lessons learned meetings. Option D: A review meeting is held to check or demonstrate deliverables.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":105,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">When a dispute arose between two important stakeholders, the project manager intervened and successfully handled it, preventing further escalation. Where should the project manager take note of the arising issue?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"When a dispute arose between two important stakeholders, the project manager intervened and successfully handled it, preventing further escalation. Where should the project manager take note of the arising issue?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Risk register<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Risk register\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Issue log<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Issue log\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Change log<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Change log\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Stakeholder register<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Stakeholder register\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The issue log is the right document to note all issues and the way they were resolved (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 185).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The issue log is the right document to note all issues and the way they were resolved (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 185).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":106,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager is trying to control the costs of the project they are working on. Thus, the project manager decides to calculate the _______________ in order to define the value of the completed work, based on its pre-approved assigned budget.<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is trying to control the costs of the project they are working on. Thus, the project manager decides to calculate the _______________ in order to define the value of the completed work, based on its pre-approved assigned budget.\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Planned Valu<span><\\/span>e<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Planned Valu e\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Earned Value<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Earned Value\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Schedule Variance<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Schedule Variance\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Cost Variance<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Cost Variance\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Earned Value (EV) refers to the value of completed work, based on the approved budget assigned to that work.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Schedule Variance (SV) is a measure of schedule performance expressed as the difference between the earned value and the Planned Value (PV).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Cost Variance (CV) is the amount of budget deficit or surplus at a given point in time, expressed as the difference between the earned value and the Actual Cost (AC).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Earned Value (EV) refers to the value of completed work, based on the approved budget assigned to that work. Option C: Schedule Variance (SV) is a measure of schedule performance expressed as the difference between the earned value and the Planned Value (PV). Option D: Cost Variance (CV) is the amount of budget deficit or surplus at a given point in time, expressed as the difference between the earned value and the Actual Cost (AC).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":107,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Which is the best communication method to maintain and improve relationships with stakeholders?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which is the best communication method to maintain and improve relationships with stakeholders?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Interactive communication<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Interactive communication\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Written communication<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Written communication\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Pull communication<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Pull communication\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Push communication<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Push communication\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Interactive communication is the most effective communication method to maintain and improve relationships with stakeholders. Interactive communication is a real-time, dynamic, two-way flow of information.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Written communication is used to exchange formal or detailed information such as decisions, statistics, facts, etc.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Pull communication, such as blog posts, is delivered from the sender to a large audience. Here information is available for people to access when they need to<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Push communication is delivered by the sender to the receiver. It is recommended when the sender sends information that does not need an immediate response from the receiver. Emails are an example of this type of communication.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Interactive communication is the most effective communication method to maintain and improve relationships with stakeholders. Interactive communication is a real-time, dynamic, two-way flow of information. Option B: Written communication is used to exchange formal or detailed information such as decisions, statistics, facts, etc. Option C: Pull communication, such as blog posts, is delivered from the sender to a large audience. Here information is available for people to access when they need to . Option D: Push communication is delivered by the sender to the receiver. It is recommended when the sender sends information that does not need an immediate response from the receiver. Emails are an example of this type of communication.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":108,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">A project team developed a detailed plan to update the operating system of all of the company's computers. Later on, the project team discovers that not every computer supports the new version of the operating system. Which of the following statements best describes this scenario? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project team developed a detailed plan to update the operating system of all of the company's computers. Later on, the project team discovers that not every computer supports the new version of the operating system. Which of the following statements best describes this scenario?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1BZ-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>The project team made a wrong assumption<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The project team made a wrong assumption\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project team didn't develop an appropriate project plan<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The project team didn't develop an appropriate project plan\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project team didn’t establish an adequate risk response<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The project team didn’t establish an adequate risk response\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The project team didn’t consider the new version of the operating system as a constraint<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The project team didn’t consider the new version of the operating system as a constraint\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2A1-0\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A3-0\\\">The project team made the assumption that all of the company’s computers are compatible with the new operating system. Consequently, they planned the project based on this belief. But later on, they found out that their assumption was untrue.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A5-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Assumptions should be logged during the project planning phase to take into consideration when creating the project plan, and that’s what the team most probably did since they developed a detailed plan. Therefore, the issue is not a result of poor planning.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A5-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> Since it wasn’t discovered during the project execution, the encountered issue wasn’t identified as a risk.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2A5-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The purpose of the project is to implement the new version of the operating system, so it cannot be considered a constraint. Yet, the hardware characteristics of the company’s computers are a constraint since they can hinder the project’s success.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The project team made the assumption that all of the company’s computers are compatible with the new operating system. Consequently, they planned the project based on this belief. But later on, they found out that their assumption was untrue. Option B: Assumptions should be logged during the project planning phase to take into consideration when creating the project plan, and that’s what the team most probably did since they developed a detailed plan. Therefore, the issue is not a result of poor planning. Option C: Since it wasn’t discovered during the project execution, the encountered issue wasn’t identified as a risk. Option D: The purpose of the project is to implement the new version of the operating system, so it cannot be considered a constraint. Yet, the hardware characteristics of the company’s computers are a constraint since they can hinder the project’s success.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":109,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">Which of the following regularly held meetings will be dedicated to tracking the project's overall progress? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following regularly held meetings will be dedicated to tracking the project's overall progress?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1BZ-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>The quality review meeting<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The quality review meeting\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The status meeting<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. The status meeting\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The kick-off meeting<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. The kick-off meeting\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The standup meeting<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. The standup meeting\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\"><span>Correct Answer = B<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\">The status meeting is a scheduled meeting that is held on a regular basis to monitor the project's progress. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The quality review meeting, as the name suggests, is meant to tackle everything related to the project quality including any issues or possible improvements. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The kick-off meeting is not a recurrent event; it’s a one-time meeting that is usually held at the end of the project planning phase and the beginning of its execution phase to officially announce its start. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Standup meetings are short, daily meetings attended by the project team to discuss what was achieved on the previous day, what issues were faced, and what is planned for the current day; they’re not meant for discussing the project’s overall progress. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The status meeting is a scheduled meeting that is held on a regular basis to monitor the project's progress. Option A: The quality review meeting, as the name suggests, is meant to tackle everything related to the project quality including any issues or possible improvements. Option C: The kick-off meeting is not a recurrent event; it’s a one-time meeting that is usually held at the end of the project planning phase and the beginning of its execution phase to officially announce its start. Option D: Standup meetings are short, daily meetings attended by the project team to discuss what was achieved on the previous day, what issues were faced, and what is planned for the current day; they’re not meant for discussing the project’s overall progress.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":110,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project manager joins a company, which has recently gone through major organizational changes. The new project manager is very concerned about the team’s lack of motivation and closely monitors when they arrive and leave work. What type of management style does the new project manager exhibit?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager joins a company, which has recently gone through major organizational changes. The new project manager is very concerned about the team’s lack of motivation and closely monitors when they arrive and leave work. What type of management style does the new project manager exhibit?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Theory X<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Theory X\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Theory Y<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Theory Y\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Theory Z<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Theory Z\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Theory XY<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Theory XY\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Douglas McGregor defined two models of worker behavior: Theory X and Theory Y. The new manager exhibits the traits of Theory X managers, who believe that the majority of people dislike work, lack motivation, and are in constant need of supervision. Theory X managers adopt an authoritarian style to make their teams work (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 160).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Douglas McGregor defined two models of worker behavior: Theory X and Theory Y. The new manager exhibits the traits of Theory X managers, who believe that the majority of people dislike work, lack motivation, and are in constant need of supervision. Theory X managers adopt an authoritarian style to make their teams work (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 160).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":111,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Which of the following meetings is process-oriented?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following meetings is process-oriented?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Sprint planning<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Sprint planning\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Sprint review<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Sprint review\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Sprint demonstratio<span><\\/span>n<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Sprint demonstratio n\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Sprint retrospective<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Sprint retrospective\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = <span><\\/span>D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Sprint Retrospective is a process-oriented meeting that is held at the end of each iteration. Its purpose is to explicitly reflect on the most significant events that have occurred during the iteration in order to make decisions on how to improve processes during the next iteration.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Options B &amp; C:<\\/span> Sprint review or demonstration, on the other hand, is a product-oriented meeting.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D Sprint Retrospective is a process-oriented meeting that is held at the end of each iteration. Its purpose is to explicitly reflect on the most significant events that have occurred during the iteration in order to make decisions on how to improve processes during the next iteration. Options B & C: Sprint review or demonstration, on the other hand, is a product-oriented meeting.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":112,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">When conducting a feasibility analysis for a project, various factors are evaluated to determine the project's viability. Which of the following variables are typically examined during this analysis? (Select three)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"When conducting a feasibility analysis for a project, various factors are evaluated to determine the project's viability. Which of the following variables are typically examined during this analysis? (Select three)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>The organization’s readiness for change<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. The organization’s readiness for change\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Budget breakdown<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Budget breakdown\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>High-level estimate of the costs<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. High-level estimate of the costs\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Team roles and responsibilities<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Team roles and responsibilities\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>Resources availability<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. Resources availability\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"C\",\"E\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A, C, E<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">When conducting a feasibility analysis for a project, several key factors are typically evaluated to determine its viability. These include:<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\">●<span>        <\\/span><span>Option A:<\\/span> Operational feasibility, which assesses the organization’s readiness for change and whether the change can be sustained post-implementation.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\">●<span>        <\\/span><span>Option C:<\\/span> Cost-effectiveness feasibility, which provides a high-level estimate of the costs and anticipated benefits of the project. This estimate offers an initial overview rather than a detailed cost-benefit analysis.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\">●<span>        <\\/span><span>Option E:<\\/span> Resource availability is considered a constraint that restricts the project viability, i.e., checking whether technical skills are available and if they can be acquired affordably.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">These variables among others help ensure a comprehensive evaluation of a project's potential success (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 86).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The feasibility study estimates the overall project cost but does not provide a detailed budget breakdown by activity or resource. This is completed during the detailed project planning phase.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The feasibility study might propose broad staffing needs but does not define specific team roles and responsibilities. This is established in the project management plan after the project is approved.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A, C, E When conducting a feasibility analysis for a project, several key factors are typically evaluated to determine its viability. These include: ● Option A: Operational feasibility, which assesses the organization’s readiness for change and whether the change can be sustained post-implementation. ● Option C: Cost-effectiveness feasibility, which provides a high-level estimate of the costs and anticipated benefits of the project. This estimate offers an initial overview rather than a detailed cost-benefit analysis. ● Option E: Resource availability is considered a constraint that restricts the project viability, i.e., checking whether technical skills are available and if they can be acquired affordably. These variables among others help ensure a comprehensive evaluation of a project's potential success (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 86). Option B: The feasibility study estimates the overall project cost but does not provide a detailed budget breakdown by activity or resource. This is completed during the detailed project planning phase. Option D: The feasibility study might propose broad staffing needs but does not define specific team roles and responsibilities. This is established in the project management plan after the project is approved.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":3},{\"n\":113,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A company is moving from a predictive approach to an adaptive approach, what does the work breakdown structure represent in an adaptive environment?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A company is moving from a predictive approach to an adaptive approach, what does the work breakdown structure represent in an adaptive environment?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-1\\\"><p><span>Sprint backlog<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Sprint backlog\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p>Product backlog <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Product backlog\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-1\\\"><p><span>Kanban board<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Kanban board\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-1\\\"><p><span>Iteration plan<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Iteration plan\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The product backlog is a prioritized list of user-centric requirements or features to be developed, similar to the WBS in that it outlines the work needed.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Sprint backlog is a list of tasks selected from the Product Backlog for a specific sprint in Scrum. It represents a subset of work for short-term focus rather than the entire project scope.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> The iteration plan is the plan for a specific iteration or sprint, focusing on the tasks and goals for that iteration rather than the entire project scope.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B The product backlog is a prioritized list of user-centric requirements or features to be developed, similar to the WBS in that it outlines the work needed. Option A: Sprint backlog is a list of tasks selected from the Product Backlog for a specific sprint in Scrum. It represents a subset of work for short-term focus rather than the entire project scope. Option D: The iteration plan is the plan for a specific iteration or sprint, focusing on the tasks and goals for that iteration rather than the entire project scope.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":114,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A vendor offers a one-time price for their service, but there is no certainty about the future continuity of their business. Which project management methodology is best suited for this situation?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A vendor offers a one-time price for their service, but there is no certainty about the future continuity of their business. Which project management methodology is best suited for this situation?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Predictive<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Predictive\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Adaptive<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Adaptive\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Incremental<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Incremental\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Sequential<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Sequential\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Adaptive methodologies, such as Agile, are designed to accommodate changes and uncertainties by allowing for iterative and incremental development. This flexibility helps manage risks and ensures the project can still progress even if the vendor's situation changes.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Predictive approach, often referred to as Waterfall, involves detailed planning and a linear approach. It is not well-suited for situations with high uncertainty because it assumes stability throughout the project<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> While the incremental approach allows for partial implementation and gradual improvements, it still requires a relatively stable environment to be most effective.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Similar to the predictive approach, this approach follows a linear, step-by-step process, making it less flexible in adapting to changes and uncertainties.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Adaptive methodologies, such as Agile, are designed to accommodate changes and uncertainties by allowing for iterative and incremental development. This flexibility helps manage risks and ensures the project can still progress even if the vendor's situation changes. Option A: Predictive approach, often referred to as Waterfall, involves detailed planning and a linear approach. It is not well-suited for situations with high uncertainty because it assumes stability throughout the project . Option C: While the incremental approach allows for partial implementation and gradual improvements, it still requires a relatively stable environment to be most effective. Option D: Similar to the predictive approach, this approach follows a linear, step-by-step process, making it less flexible in adapting to changes and uncertainties.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":115,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">What should the project manager check to learn more about the product’s quality requirements necessary for establishing quality metrics?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What should the project manager check to learn more about the product’s quality requirements necessary for establishing quality metrics?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Requirements traceability matrix<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Requirements traceability matrix\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Requirement management plan<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Requirement management plan\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>Requirement documentation<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Requirement documentation\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>Quality management plan<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Quality management plan\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Requirements documents capture and manage all product requirements and relevant information, serving as a comprehensive record for product development and management.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The requirements traceability matrix ensures that each solution requirement is valuable and within scope by linking it to business needs, goals, and project objectives. It does not contain detailed quality requirements.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The requirements management plan outlines how requirements will be managed along the project. It does not provide specific quality requirements.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Quality management plan outlines how policies, procedures, and guidelines will be applied to meet the quality objectives rather than describes the product quality requirements.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Requirements documents capture and manage all product requirements and relevant information, serving as a comprehensive record for product development and management. Option A: The requirements traceability matrix ensures that each solution requirement is valuable and within scope by linking it to business needs, goals, and project objectives. It does not contain detailed quality requirements. Option B: The requirements management plan outlines how requirements will be managed along the project. It does not provide specific quality requirements. Option D: Quality management plan outlines how policies, procedures, and guidelines will be applied to meet the quality objectives rather than describes the product quality requirements.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":116,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">When enabling the organization transition, what artifacts should be elaborated? (Select three)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"When enabling the organization transition, what artifacts should be elaborated? (Select three)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s79\\\"><p><span>Readiness assessment plan<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Readiness assessment plan\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s79\\\"><p><span>Transition matrix<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Transition matrix\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s7E\\\"><p><span>Transition plan<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Transition plan\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s7H\\\"><p><span>Transition strategy<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Transition strategy\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s79\\\"><p><span>Transition impact analysis<\\/span><span><\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Transition impact analysis\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"C\",\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A, C, D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The transition approach includes a readiness assessment plan, transition strategy, and transition plan (Business Analysis for Practitioners, page 82).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Readiness Assessment Plan:<\\/span> This plan evaluates the organization's preparedness for transitioning to a new state by assessing its capability and willingness. It typically includes a readiness checklist and answers key questions such as:<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\">●<span>        <\\/span>What aspects of organizational readiness will be measured?<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\">●<span>        <\\/span>How will readiness be assessed?<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\">●<span>        <\\/span>What are the roles and responsibilities involved in readiness assessment?<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\"><span>Transition Plan<\\/span>:<span> This document outlines the tasks needed to achieve a <\\/span>successful transition, including their deadlines, required resources, and the sequence of activities. It ensures that all necessary steps are completed in an organized manner.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\"><span>Transition Strategy:<\\/span> A well-defined transition strategy is crucial for a successful transition. It includes various approaches like:<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\">●<span>        <\\/span>Massive, one-time cutover<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\">●<span>        <\\/span>Segmented cutover<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\">●<span>        <\\/span>Timeboxed coexistence<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\">●<span>        <\\/span>Permanent coexistence<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Options B &amp; E:<\\/span> Transition matrix and Transition impact analysis are made-up terms.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A, C, D The transition approach includes a readiness assessment plan, transition strategy, and transition plan (Business Analysis for Practitioners, page 82). Readiness Assessment Plan: This plan evaluates the organization's preparedness for transitioning to a new state by assessing its capability and willingness. It typically includes a readiness checklist and answers key questions such as: ● What aspects of organizational readiness will be measured? ● How will readiness be assessed? ● What are the roles and responsibilities involved in readiness assessment? Transition Plan : This document outlines the tasks needed to achieve a successful transition, including their deadlines, required resources, and the sequence of activities. It ensures that all necessary steps are completed in an organized manner. Transition Strategy: A well-defined transition strategy is crucial for a successful transition. It includes various approaches like: ● Massive, one-time cutover ● Segmented cutover ● Timeboxed coexistence ● Permanent coexistence Options B & E: Transition matrix and Transition impact analysis are made-up terms.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":3},{\"n\":117,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">While leading the construction of New York's new bridge, the project manager was informed by one of the subject matter experts that, next July, all of the bridge construction work will need to stop taking into consideration the past history of river flooding due to hurricane season. Thus, the project manager agrees with the expert and decides to stop work during that month. This decision is considered as:<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"While leading the construction of New York's new bridge, the project manager was informed by one of the subject matter experts that, next July, all of the bridge construction work will need to stop taking into consideration the past history of river flooding due to hurricane season. Thus, the project manager agrees with the expert and decides to stop work during that month. This decision is considered as:\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Acceptance​<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Acceptance\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Transfer<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Transfer\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Mitigation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Mitigation\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>​Avoidance<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Avoidance\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = <span><\\/span>D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">The project manager’s decision to stop construction work during July means that they’re trying to avoid the risk rather than accept it. The project manager made the safe decision to stop all construction work during hurricane season to avoid the risk of financial loss or putting the project staff in danger. This risk response is suitable for threats of high priority, high probability of occurrence, and a considerable negative impact.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The decision can not be to mitigate because mitigation implies that the project manager would attempt to reduce the threat’s probability of occurrence and/or impact, which can’t be done since they have no control over river floods, nor did they take any prior action to mitigate its damage if it does occur (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 123).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D The project manager’s decision to stop construction work during July means that they’re trying to avoid the risk rather than accept it. The project manager made the safe decision to stop all construction work during hurricane season to avoid the risk of financial loss or putting the project staff in danger. This risk response is suitable for threats of high priority, high probability of occurrence, and a considerable negative impact. Option C: The decision can not be to mitigate because mitigation implies that the project manager would attempt to reduce the threat’s probability of occurrence and/or impact, which can’t be done since they have no control over river floods, nor did they take any prior action to mitigate its damage if it does occur (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 123).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":118,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">A project manager has been assigned to a project that consists of constructing a bridge in their city. Missing the deadline for the project completion would make the company pay a fine for each additional day of delay. Which of the following does this example best illustrate? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager has been assigned to a project that consists of constructing a bridge in their city. Missing the deadline for the project completion would make the company pay a fine for each additional day of delay. Which of the following does this example best illustrate?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1BZ-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>Assumption<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Assumption\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Cost constraint<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Cost constraint\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Critical path method planning<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Critical path method planning\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Schedule constraint<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Schedule constraint\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\"><span>Correct Answer = D<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\">The situation describes a schedule constraint: the project needs to be completed within deadlines or else the company will be obliged to pay a daily fine. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D The situation describes a schedule constraint: the project needs to be completed within deadlines or else the company will be obliged to pay a daily fine.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":119,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">A project manager is assigned to a construction project. During the last planning session, the project team finished decomposing the project deliverables. Which of the following documents was produced during this meeting? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is assigned to a construction project. During the last planning session, the project team finished decomposing the project deliverables. Which of the following documents was produced during this meeting?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1BZ-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>    <\\/span>Work Breakdown Structure (WBS)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Work Breakdown Structure (WBS)\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Organizational Breakdown Structure (OBS)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Organizational Breakdown Structure (OBS)\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Resource breakdown structure<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Resource breakdown structure\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s1C1-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Requirements documentation<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Requirements documentation\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\"><span>Correct Answer = A<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\">The process of breaking down project deliverables means the creation of the project Work Breakdown Structure (WBS). <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> The Organizational Breakdown Structure (OBS) represents a breakdown of the project's hierarchy. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option C:<\\/span> The resource breakdown structure includes the composition of the project team. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Requirements documentation is a record of product requirements and the relevant information needed to manage those requirements. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A The process of breaking down project deliverables means the creation of the project Work Breakdown Structure (WBS). Option B: The Organizational Breakdown Structure (OBS) represents a breakdown of the project's hierarchy. Option C: The resource breakdown structure includes the composition of the project team. Option D: Requirements documentation is a record of product requirements and the relevant information needed to manage those requirements.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":120,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Which of the following elicitation techniques are intended to reach a large number of stakeholders? (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following elicitation techniques are intended to reach a large number of stakeholders? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Focus groups<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Focus groups\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Document analysis<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Document analysis\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Interviews<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Interviews\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Surveys<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Surveys\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>Prototyping<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. Prototyping\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A, D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Focus groups gather prequalified stakeholders and subject matter experts (SMEs) to discuss their expectations and attitudes toward a proposed solution. They offer valuable feedback directly from customers and end users, providing insights into their perspectives and needs. A survey is a structured set of questions aimed at efficiently gathering information from a large group of respondents.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Document analysis is an elicitation technique that involves reviewing and examining existing documentation to extract and identify information about the product. When using this technique, it's important to assess the accuracy and relevance of the information, as outdated or current documents might reflect constraints that no longer apply.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A, D Focus groups gather prequalified stakeholders and subject matter experts (SMEs) to discuss their expectations and attitudes toward a proposed solution. They offer valuable feedback directly from customers and end users, providing insights into their perspectives and needs. A survey is a structured set of questions aimed at efficiently gathering information from a large group of respondents. Option B: Document analysis is an elicitation technique that involves reviewing and examining existing documentation to extract and identify information about the product. When using this technique, it's important to assess the accuracy and relevance of the information, as outdated or current documents might reflect constraints that no longer apply.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":121,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A business analyst has just completed the requirements elicitation, what should the business analyst do next?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A business analyst has just completed the requirements elicitation, what should the business analyst do next?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Validate requirement<span><\\/span>s<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Validate requirement s\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Select and approve requirements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Select and approve requirements\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Confirm elicitation results<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Confirm elicitation results\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Verify requirements<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Verify requirements\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">After elicitation, a business analyst should confirm the gathered elicitation results with stakeholders, ensuring they accurately reflect stakeholder needs and expectations<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Options A, B, D:<\\/span> After confirming elicitation results, requirements will be verified, validated, then selected and approved (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 24).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C After elicitation, a business analyst should confirm the gathered elicitation results with stakeholders, ensuring they accurately reflect stakeholder needs and expectations . Options A, B, D: After confirming elicitation results, requirements will be verified, validated, then selected and approved (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 24).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":122,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">During the project charter development phase, the project manager discovered a gap in the business case; some key regulatory requirements were missing. Non-compliance with these regulations could result in legal issues. Complying with these regulations, on the other hand, could result in drastic scope changes and budget overruns. What should the project manager do?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"During the project charter development phase, the project manager discovered a gap in the business case; some key regulatory requirements were missing. Non-compliance with these regulations could result in legal issues. Complying with these regulations, on the other hand, could result in drastic scope changes and budget overruns. What should the project manager do?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Issue a change request to implement the needed changes to meet regulations<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Issue a change request to implement the needed changes to meet regulations\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Consider these findings a risk and plan a response<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Consider these findings a risk and plan a response\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Start implementing the project and decide later on how to address these requirements when a better solution can be established<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Start implementing the project and decide later on how to address these requirements when a better solution can be established\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Inform the project sponsor of their findings<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Inform the project sponsor of their findings\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9D-0\\\">The project manager should immediately inform the project sponsor of their findings. The PMI's Code of Ethics requires project managers to comply with all laws and regulations. Concealing such information can lead the organization to face legal issues. In the case of a predictive project, change requests can be only issued after setting the project baseline. In the described scenario, the project is neither authorized nor baselined since it’s still in the project charter development phase.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D The project manager should immediately inform the project sponsor of their findings. The PMI's Code of Ethics requires project managers to comply with all laws and regulations. Concealing such information can lead the organization to face legal issues. In the case of a predictive project, change requests can be only issued after setting the project baseline. In the described scenario, the project is neither authorized nor baselined since it’s still in the project charter development phase.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":123,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A project team is assessing which agile methodology to use when a team member suggested working with the Feature Driven Development approach (FDD). What are the FDD activities? (Select three)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project team is assessing which agile methodology to use when a team member suggested working with the Feature Driven Development approach (FDD). What are the FDD activities? (Select three)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Develop an overall model<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Develop an overall model\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Visualize and limit work in progress<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Visualize and limit work in progress\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Build a features list<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Build a features list\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Design by feature<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Design by feature\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>E.<\\/span><span>      <\\/span>Apply cadence<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"E. Apply cadence\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"C\",\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A, C, D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Developing an overall model involves creating a high-level model of the system to guide the development process and ensure that all stakeholders have a common understanding of the system architecture. Building a feature list involves identifying and listing all the features to be developed. Each feature represents a small, valuable piece of functionality from the user's perspective. Each feature is designed, built, and tested in its own iteration, ensuring that the development process is manageable and structured.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Visualizing and limiting work in progress is a practice associated with Kanban, focusing on managing workflow and work-in-progress limits.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option E:<\\/span> While cadence (regular, predictable intervals) is important in many Agile methodologies, it is more closely associated with Scrum, where sprints or iterations have a consistent duration.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A, C, D Developing an overall model involves creating a high-level model of the system to guide the development process and ensure that all stakeholders have a common understanding of the system architecture. Building a feature list involves identifying and listing all the features to be developed. Each feature represents a small, valuable piece of functionality from the user's perspective. Each feature is designed, built, and tested in its own iteration, ensuring that the development process is manageable and structured. Option B: Visualizing and limiting work in progress is a practice associated with Kanban, focusing on managing workflow and work-in-progress limits. Option E: While cadence (regular, predictable intervals) is important in many Agile methodologies, it is more closely associated with Scrum, where sprints or iterations have a consistent duration.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":3},{\"n\":124,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A project manager managing a national book fair identified some low-impact risks early in the planning phase. What should the project manager do next?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager managing a national book fair identified some low-impact risks early in the planning phase. What should the project manager do next?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s82-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Ignore the risks since their impact is fairly low<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Ignore the risks since their impact is fairly low\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Add the risks to the risk register and keep monitoring them<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Add the risks to the risk register and keep monitoring them\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Develop a detailed risk response<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Develop a detailed risk response\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_sR-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Report the risks to the fair sponsor(s)<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Report the risks to the fair sponsor(s)\"}],\"key\":[\"B\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = B<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Passive risk acceptance is an appropriate approach for low-impact risks. No proactive action is needed for passive acceptance other than periodically reviewing the threat to ensure that it is not signiﬁcantly changing. On the other hand, active risk acceptance entails developing a detailed risk response or a contingency plan that would be implemented if the event occurred (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 123).<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = B Passive risk acceptance is an appropriate approach for low-impact risks. No proactive action is needed for passive acceptance other than periodically reviewing the threat to ensure that it is not signiﬁcantly changing. On the other hand, active risk acceptance entails developing a detailed risk response or a contingency plan that would be implemented if the event occurred (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, page 123).\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":125,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Maria is supervising three projects within her organization: two are of a similar type, while the third is entirely different. What is Maria’s role in the organization?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Maria is supervising three projects within her organization: two are of a similar type, while the third is entirely different. What is Maria’s role in the organization?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project coordinator<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Project coordinator\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Project manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Project manager\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Program manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Program manager\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Portfolio manager<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Portfolio manager\"}],\"key\":[\"D\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = D<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A portfolio manager coordinates and manages a group of related or non-related projects and programs.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = D A portfolio manager coordinates and manages a group of related or non-related projects and programs.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":126,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Which of the following is an example of an information radiator?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Which of the following is an example of an information radiator?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Prototyp<span><\\/span>e<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Prototyp e\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Milestone<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Milestone\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Kanban board<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Kanban board\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Brainstorming<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Brainstorming\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Information radiators, such as the Kanban board, are a visible display of up-to-date information concerning the team’s work status.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> Prototype is a method of getting early feedback on requirements.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> A milestone is a point or an event in the project that does not display status information<span><\\/span>.<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Brainstorming is a data-gathering technique.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C Information radiators, such as the Kanban board, are a visible display of up-to-date information concerning the team’s work status. Option A: Prototype is a method of getting early feedback on requirements. Option B: A milestone is a point or an event in the project that does not display status information . Option D: Brainstorming is a data-gathering technique.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":127,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">Since leadership is crucial for project success, a project manager joins a training program to learn how to become a good leader. Which of the following activities should the project manager learn to apply in order to become the leader they aspire to be?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"Since leadership is crucial for project success, a project manager joins a training program to learn how to become a good leader. Which of the following activities should the project manager learn to apply in order to become the leader they aspire to be?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2Z-1\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Guiding, motivating, and directing the project team<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Guiding, motivating, and directing the project team\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Improving their project’s performance<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Improving their project’s performance\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Learning more about the specific domain of their project to be able to technically support the project team<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. Learning more about the specific domain of their project to be able to technically support the project team\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2N-1\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Learning more about project management by obtaining a PMP certification<\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Learning more about project management by obtaining a PMP certification\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Leadership skills involve the ability to guide, motivate, and direct a team. This skill set may also include negotiation, assertiveness, communication, critical thinking, problem-solving, and interpersonal skills (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, pages 23-25).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Options B, C, D:<\\/span> Improving the project’s performance, learning more about the specific domain of the project, and obtaining a PMP certification can make the project manager a better manager rather than a better leader.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A Leadership skills involve the ability to guide, motivate, and direct a team. This skill set may also include negotiation, assertiveness, communication, critical thinking, problem-solving, and interpersonal skills (PMBOK Guide 7th Edition, pages 23-25). Options B, C, D: Improving the project’s performance, learning more about the specific domain of the project, and obtaining a PMP certification can make the project manager a better manager rather than a better leader.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":128,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">A project manager has been requested to present the roles and responsibilities of their team members during the next meeting with the senior management. Which of the following should the project manager bring to the meeting? <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager has been requested to present the roles and responsibilities of their team members during the next meeting with the senior management. Which of the following should the project manager bring to the meeting?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3C-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Resource Histogram <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. Resource Histogram\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Hierarchy Chart <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. Hierarchy Chart\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>RACI Chart <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. RACI Chart\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>Gantt Chart <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. Gantt Chart\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\"><span>Correct Answer = C<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\">RACI charts are a type of RAM chart, which show the project resources assigned to each work package and illustrate the connections between work packages or activities, and project team members. RACI stands for the different responsibility types: Responsible, Accountable, Consulted, and Informed. A RACI chart is used to ensure the clear assignment of roles and responsibilities within the team. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option A:<\\/span> The Resource Histogram provides information about resource usage over time. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option B:<\\/span> Hierarchy charts represent the organization's structure and illustrate the reporting relationships and chains of command within the organization. <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9M-0\\\"><span>Option D:<\\/span> Gantt charts represent schedule information by listing activities, dates, and activity durations in a bar chart. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C RACI charts are a type of RAM chart, which show the project resources assigned to each work package and illustrate the connections between work packages or activities, and project team members. RACI stands for the different responsibility types: Responsible, Accountable, Consulted, and Informed. A RACI chart is used to ensure the clear assignment of roles and responsibilities within the team. Option A: The Resource Histogram provides information about resource usage over time. Option B: Hierarchy charts represent the organization's structure and illustrate the reporting relationships and chains of command within the organization. Option D: Gantt charts represent schedule information by listing activities, dates, and activity durations in a bar chart.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":129,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s38-0\\\">__ is the float of activities on the critical path. <\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"__ is the float of activities on the critical path.\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3C-0\\\"><span>A.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>0 <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"A. 0\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>B.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>1 <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"B. 1\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>C.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>2 <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"C. 2\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s3F-0\\\"><span>D.<\\/span><span>     <\\/span>It depends on the dependencies and duration of each activity  <\\/p>\",\"text\":\"D. It depends on the dependencies and duration of each activity\"}],\"key\":[\"A\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\"><span>Correct Answer = A<\\/span> <\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s9R-0\\\">On a critical path, the float of activities is zero. Float, often known as slack, is how long an activity can be delayed without causing the whole project to be delayed. <\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A On a critical path, the float of activities is zero. Float, often known as slack, is how long an activity can be delayed without causing the whole project to be delayed.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":130,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">What is the primary purpose of a Business Requirements Document (BRD)?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"What is the primary purpose of a Business Requirements Document (BRD)?\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>To outline the project's budget and timeline.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"To outline the project's budget and timeline.\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>To define the technical specifications of the solution.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"To define the technical specifications of the solution.\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-0\\\"><p><span>To document the business needs and goals for a project.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"To document the business needs and goals for a project.\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\"><p><span>To create a detailed work breakdown structure.<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"To create a detailed work breakdown structure.\"}],\"key\":[\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A Business Requirements Document (BRD) focuses on capturing the business requirements, objectives, and the reasons behind the project (Business Analysis for Practitioners, page 73)<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Options A, B, D:<\\/span> The Business Requirements Document (BRD) does not detail technical specifications, budget, timeline, or a work breakdown structure.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = C A Business Requirements Document (BRD) focuses on capturing the business requirements, objectives, and the reasons behind the project (Business Analysis for Practitioners, page 73) Options A, B, D: The Business Requirements Document (BRD) does not detail technical specifications, budget, timeline, or a work breakdown structure.\",\"type\":\"single\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":null},{\"n\":131,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2X-0\\\">A business analyst is facilitating the development of the product roadmap. What tools and techniques will the business analyst use? (Select two)<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A business analyst is facilitating the development of the product roadmap. What tools and techniques will the business analyst use? (Select two)\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"A\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Story Mapping<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Story Mapping\"},{\"id\":\"B\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Interviews<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Interviews\"},{\"id\":\"C\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4A-2\\\"><p>Product visioning <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Product visioning\"},{\"id\":\"D\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s4D-0\\\" id=\\\"page_151\\\"><p><span>Market analysis<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Market analysis\"},{\"id\":\"E\",\"html\":\"<li class=\\\"class_s45-0\\\"><p><span>Competitive analysis<\\/span> <\\/p><\\/li>\",\"text\":\"Competitive analysis\"}],\"key\":[\"A\",\"C\"],\"answerHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s9B-1\\\">Correct Answer = A, C<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">Developing a product roadmap involves creating a high-level plan that outlines the key features of a product that are scheduled for delivery over multiple iterations/releases. Product visioning is a technique that facilitates the development of the roadmap as it establishes the overall direction. Story mapping is another technique used to organize user stories based on their business value and the typical order in which users interact with them. This helps teams achieve a shared understanding of <span><\\/span>what needs to be built and the sequence in which it should be developed (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 95).<\\/p><p class=\\\"class_s80-0\\\"><span>Options B, D, E:<\\/span> Interviews, Market analysis, and Competitive analysis are not techniques used for the facilitation of the product roadmap.<\\/p>\",\"answerText\":\"Correct Answer = A, C Developing a product roadmap involves creating a high-level plan that outlines the key features of a product that are scheduled for delivery over multiple iterations/releases. Product visioning is a technique that facilitates the development of the roadmap as it establishes the overall direction. Story mapping is another technique used to organize user stories based on their business value and the typical order in which users interact with them. This helps teams achieve a shared understanding of what needs to be built and the sequence in which it should be developed (PMI Guide to Business Analysis, page 95). Options B, D, E: Interviews, Market analysis, and Competitive analysis are not techniques used for the facilitation of the product roadmap.\",\"type\":\"multi\",\"special\":null,\"manual\":false,\"sourceIssue\":\"\",\"selectCount\":2},{\"n\":132,\"stemHtml\":\"<p class=\\\"class_s2J-1\\\">A project manager is leading a team of 6 members in an open-space work environment. While working on an offer, the potential client called to request a cost estimate. The project manager informed the client that it was around $600,000. However, a team member immediately corrected the project manager, saying “It’s actually around $700,000”. The project manager didn’t realize that the team member was overhearing the discussion. What kind of communication is being used here?<\\/p>\",\"stemText\":\"A project manager is leading a team of 6 membe";
